    "id": "madas/as-pure-u/q11",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-u/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The point A has coordinates ( 2,1 . − ) a) Find the coordinates of the point of reflection of A about the straight line with equation 3 x y 12 . 6 + = ( ) The point P , whose coordinates are ( 4,2 , is rotated about A by 90° anticlockwise, ) onto the point Q . b) Determine the coordinates of Q . 8 ( )\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
